  "review": {
    "book": "2SA",
    "entityID": "person:mephibosheth_1999",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA4:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Jonathan, Saul’s son, had a son who was lame in his feet. He was five years old when the news came about Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel; and his nurse picked him up and fled. As she hurried to flee, he fell and became lame. His name was Mephibosheth."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, the son of Saul, came to David, fell on his face, and showed respect. David said, “Mephibosheth?” He answered, “Behold, your servant!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "Till the land for him—you, your sons, and your servants. Bring in the harvest, that your master’s son may have bread to eat; but Mephibosheth your master’s son will always eat bread at my table.” Now Ziba had fifteen sons and twenty servants."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Ziba said to the king, “According to all that my lord the king commands his servant, so your servant will do.” So Mephibosheth ate at the king’s table like one of the king’s sons."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Mephibosheth had a young son, whose name was Mica. All who lived in Ziba’s house were servants to Mephibosheth."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Mephibosheth lived in Jerusalem, for he ate continually at the king’s table. He was lame in both his feet."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "When David was a little past the top, behold, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth met him with a couple of donkeys saddled, and on them two hundred loaves of bread, and one hundred clusters of raisins, and one hundred summer fruits, and a container of wine."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then the king said to Ziba, “Behold, all that belongs to Mephibosheth is yours.” Ziba said, “I bow down. Let me find favor in your sight, my lord, O king.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA19:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Mephibosheth the son of Saul came down to meet the king; and he had neither groomed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes, from the day the king departed until the day he came home in peace."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA19:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "When he had come to Jerusalem to meet the king, the king said to him, “Why didn’t you go with me, Mephibosheth?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA19:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "Mephibosheth said to the king, “Yes, let him take all, because my lord the king has come in peace to his own house.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA21:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "But the king spared Mephibosheth the son of Jonathan the son of Saul, because of the LORD’s oath that was between them, between David and Jonathan the son of Saul."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said, “Is there yet any who is left of Saul’s house, that I may show him kindness for Jonathan’s sake?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA9:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said to him, “Don’t be afraid, for I will surely show you kindness for Jonathan your father’s sake, and will restore to you all the land of Saul your father. You will eat bread at my table continually.”"
      }
    ],
